# The WAL robustness tester (`examples/etcd/wal`), the part's translation: package initialization

The part `LinuxFs/`'s copy of the main tree's `Base.lean` (W4c U1, 2026-11-14,
`notes/wal-fsext-w4c-plan.md`). The tester has no package variable and no `init()`: its fact is
`True`, and its initializer initializes its imports (`Init.lean`, generated by `etc/gen-init.py`,
`LFS_PKGS`). The instances of its imports are imported here: `wal`'s, `fileutil`'s, `walpb`'s, zap's
and the standard library's through the part's `wal/PkgInit.lean`, `raftpb`'s through the part's raft
root (`go_etcd_io/raft/v3/PkgInit.lean`), and `durable`'s.
-/
